From 0b1c9eefb584cd037a1fdeb55800ec8e63043674 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The FBC Agent <thefbcspecialagent@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:02:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] input: SDL2 game controllers on Windows too (XBOX_SDL_WINDOW)

With XBOX_SDL_WINDOW the Windows build reads its pads through SDL's game
controller API instead of XInput, the backend macOS and Linux already used,
so one map serves every host and any controller SDL knows works. The
keyboard and the mouse+keyboard pad merge as before.

The SDL backend now also opens its controllers: nothing called
xbox_InputInit, so before this the POSIX build never opened one.
xbox_InputInit (or the first poll) brings them up once; an empty port is
scanned again at most once a second (plug in / pull out while running).
Pads are locked against a rescan from another thread. On Windows the pads
read in the background as XInput did, device arrival goes to SDL's own
joystick thread, the events are ignored (the state is polled) and the
input layer updates them itself: the window runs on its own thread there.

Logs [PAD] lines for a pad opened or gone and for Back+Start held together.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ahYm8JBvCH5KhgtSu9Yoy
